<file path="docs/mermaid/battle_rts/08_STATE_AND_DATA_FLOW.md">
# RTS State And Data Flow

## Purpose

This file answers one question: where does the state live, and who mutates it?

## State Ownership

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    UI["BattleCommandOverlay
    selection state
    transient UI state"] --> CMD["BattleCommander.BattleGroup
    command
    target_x/y
    formation
    charge_state"]

    CMD --> AI["BattleSimpleAI
    decision logic
    timers
    phase state
    objectives"]

    AI --> UNITS["BattleUnitSystem
    x y vx vy
    hp morale
    target_unit
    group_id
    ability state"]

    AI --> PROJ["BattleProjectileSystem
    projectile SoA"]

    ARENA["BattleArena
    blocked tiles
    battle config
    player ref
    wave state
    UI refs"] --> AI
    ARENA --> UNITS
    ARENA --> PROJ

    FLOW["BattleFlowField
    objective fields
    LOS
    avoidance"] --> AI
```

## Data Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Player input"] --> B["BattleCommandOverlay selection state"]
    B --> C["command_issued(group_id, cmd, x, y)"]
    C --> D["battle_arena.gd::_on_command_issued()"]
    D --> E["BattleGroup.command / target_x / target_y"]
    E --> F["battle_simple_ai.gd::update()"]
    F --> G["BattleUnitSystem target_unit / vx / vy / morale / ability flags"]
    F --> H["BattleProjectileSystem.spawn()"]
    G --> I["battle_arena.gd::_update_unit_physics()"]
    H --> J["battle_projectile_system.gd::update()"]
    J --> K["BattleUnitSystem.damage()"]
```

## Primary Data Carriers

### Group intent

- [battle_commander.gd#L9](/Users/developer-cloudprimero/Desktop/Godot/new-game-project/scripts/battle/battle_commander.gd#L9)
- fields:
  - `command`
  - `target_group_id`
  - `formation_type`
  - `target_x`
  - `target_y`
  - `charge_state`
  - `initial_size`

### Unit runtime state

- [battle_unit_system.gd#L151](/Users/developer-cloudprimero/Desktop/Godot/new-game-project/scripts/battle/battle_unit_system.gd#L151)
- high-value arrays:
  - `x`, `y`, `vx`, `vy`
  - `group_id`
  - `target_unit`
  - `morale`
  - `ability_cooldown`, `ability_timer`, `ability_active`
  - `is_commander`, `commander_debuff_timer`
  - `formation_bonus_active`, `group_formation`
  - `charge_time`
  - `scatter_time`, `saved_group_id`

### Arena-owned external state

- [battle_arena.gd#L47](/Users/developer-cloudprimero/Desktop/Godot/new-game-project/scripts/battle/battle_arena.gd#L47)
- high-value fields:
  - `units`
  - `projectiles`
  - `commander`
  - `ai`
  - `_blocked_tiles`
  - `_config`
  - `command_mode`
  - `_pending_red_waves`

### AI-owned strategic state

- [battle_simple_ai.gd#L14](/Users/developer-cloudprimero/Desktop/Godot/new-game-project/scripts/battle/battle_simple_ai.gd#L14)
- high-value fields:
  - `_battle_time`
  - `_retarget_timer`
  - `_strategy_timer`
  - `_army_phase`
  - `red_objective`, `blue_objective`
  - `player_position`, `player_alive`
  - `_blue_cavalry_ratio`, `_blue_heavy_ratio`

## Mutation Map

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    OVL["Overlay"] -->|writes| G1["BattleGroup.command"]
    OVL -->|writes| G2["BattleGroup.target_x/y"]
    OVL -->|sometimes rewrites| U1["BattleUnitSystem.group_id"]

    ARENA["BattleArena"] -->|writes| G1
    ARENA -->|clears| U2["BattleUnitSystem.target_unit"]
    ARENA -->|bridges| U3["BattleUnitSystem.hp / alive / morale"]
    ARENA -->|bridges| P1["BattleProjectileSystem.alive"]

    AI["BattleSimpleAI"] -->|writes| U2
    AI -->|writes| U4["BattleUnitSystem.vx/vy/facing"]
    AI -->|writes| U5["BattleUnitSystem.morale"]
    AI -->|writes| U6["BattleUnitSystem.ability_*"]
    AI -->|spawns| P2["Projectiles"]

    PROJ["ProjectileSystem"] -->|calls| DMG["BattleUnitSystem.damage()"]
    DMG -->|writes| U3
```

## High Stakes State

These are the fields that connect multiple subsystems and are easiest to break:

- `BattleGroup.command`
- `BattleGroup.target_x / target_y`
- `BattleUnitSystem.group_id`
- `BattleUnitSystem.target_unit`
- `BattleUnitSystem.morale`
- `BattleUnitSystem.ability_active`
- `BattleUnitSystem.group_formation`
- `BattleProjectileSystem.source_formation`

If you change those, read the AI loop and arena frame loop again before committing.
</file>

<file path="docs/mermaid/battle_rts/09_CONTROL_FLOW.md">
# RTS Control Flow

## Purpose

This file shows how control actually moves through the battle code each frame.

## Top Level Frame Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["_physics_process(delta)
    battle_arena.gd#L1192"] --> B["units.build_spatial_hash()"]
    B --> C["units.update_formation_bonuses()
    every N frames"]
    C --> D["ai.update(dt)"]
    D --> E["projectiles.update(dt, units, blocked_tiles)"]
    E --> F["_check_soa_projectiles_vs_player()"]
    F --> G["_check_player_bullets_vs_soa()"]
    G --> H["collision.resolve(units, dt, blocked_tiles)"]
    H --> I["_resolve_player_unit_collision()"]
    I --> J["_check_player_abilities_vs_soa()"]
    J --> K["_update_unit_physics()"]
    K --> L["victory / waves / hud / fog / renderer"]
```

## Per-Unit Decision Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["ai.update()
    per-unit loop"] --> B{"alive?"}
    B -->|no| Z["skip"]
    B -->|yes| C["burn / debuff / stagger / scatter checks"]
    C --> D["ability update"]
    D --> E{"route?"}
    E -->|yes| R["_do_rout()"]
    E -->|no| F["read group_id and BattleGroup.command"]
    F --> G["optional group cohesion"]
    G --> H{"command"}
    H -->|MOVE| I["_do_movement_toward_pos()
    clear target_unit"]
    H -->|ATTACK| J["_update_target()
    move+attack toward command target"]
    H -->|HOLD| K["_do_attack_any()"]
    H -->|DEFENSIVE| L["_do_cluster()
    _do_attack_any()"]
    H -->|SCATTER| M["_do_scatter()
    _do_combat()"]
    H -->|FOLLOW| N["_do_follow_player()"]
    H -->|CHARGE| O["_do_movement_toward_pos()
    speed boost
    _do_attack_any()"]
    H -->|RETREAT| P["_do_rout_retreat()
    limited attack"]
```

## Command Ingress Flow

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["Mouse / keyboard"] --> B["battle_command_overlay.gd::_input()"]
    B --> C["_issue_command_to_selection()"]
    C --> D["command_issued signal"]
    D --> E["battle_arena.gd::_on_command_issued()"]
    E --> F["BattleGroup.command = cmd"]
    E --> G["BattleGroup.target_x/y = world pos"]
    E --> H["clear units.target_unit"]
    F --> I["ai.update() sees new command next frame"]
```

## Attack Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["_update_target()"] --> B["_do_attack()"]
    B --> C{"in range and LOS?"}
    C -->|no| Z["no attack"]
    C -->|yes| D["morale + commander + formation modifiers"]
    D --> E["projectiles.spawn()"]
    E --> F["battle_projectile_system.gd::update()"]
    F --> G["BattleUnitSystem.damage()"]
    G --> H["hp / morale / alive change"]
```

## Player Bridge Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Player bullets"] --> B["_check_player_bullets_vs_soa()"]
    B --> C["units.damage()"]

    D["SoA projectiles"] --> E["_check_soa_projectiles_vs_player()"]
    E --> F["player.take_damage()"]

    G["Player body collision"] --> H["_resolve_player_unit_collision()"]
    H --> I["units.damage()"]
    H --> J["player.take_damage()"]

    K["Player dash / abilities"] --> L["_check_player_abilities_vs_soa()"]
    L --> M["units.damage() / knockback"]
```

## Exact Control Hubs

- [battle_arena.gd#L1192](/Users/developer-cloudprimero/Desktop/Godot/new-game-project/scripts/battle/battle_arena.gd#L1192): frame orchestrator
- [battle_simple_ai.gd#L281](/Users/developer-cloudprimero/Desktop/Godot/new-game-project/scripts/battle/battle_simple_ai.gd#L281): AI root
- [battle_simple_ai.gd#L428](/Users/developer-cloudprimero/Desktop/Godot/new-game-project/scripts/battle/battle_simple_ai.gd#L428): command dispatch
- [battle_simple_ai.gd#L2179](/Users/developer-cloudprimero/Desktop/Godot/new-game-project/scripts/battle/battle_simple_ai.gd#L2179): movement hub
- [battle_simple_ai.gd#L2283](/Users/developer-cloudprimero/Desktop/Godot/new-game-project/scripts/battle/battle_simple_ai.gd#L2283): attack hub

## Reading Advice

When the behavior is surprising, ask these questions in order:

1. what command was written into `BattleGroup`?
2. what did `ai.update()` do with that command?
3. what state did it write into `BattleUnitSystem`?
4. what did the frame loop do after that?
</file>

