<file path="docs/design/ITEM_AND_MUTATION_SYSTEM.md">
# Item & Mutation System

## Purpose
Equipment defines hero capability. Mutations modify behavior in stackable, combinatorial ways. Together they create emergent build diversity — the core of replayability.

## Equipment Slots

```
┌──────────────┐
│   WEAPON     │  Primary attack pattern (projectile type, rate, damage)
├──────────────┤
│   ARMOR      │  Defense, HP, resistance modifiers
├──────────────┤
│   ARTIFACT   │  Active ability (cooldown-based)
├──────────────┤
│  CORE MODULE │  Passive system modifier (economy, companion, mutation boost)
└──────────────┘
```

## Data Models

### EquipmentDefinition
```
class_name EquipmentDefinition extends Resource

enum Slot { WEAPON, ARMOR, ARTIFACT, CORE_MODULE }
enum Rarity { COMMON, UNCOMMON, RARE, EPIC, LEGENDARY }

var item_id: String              # unique key
var item_name: String
var description: String
var slot: Slot
var rarity: Rarity
var icon: Texture2D
var stat_modifiers: Array[StatModifier] = []
var innate_mutations: Array[MutationDefinition] = []
var weapon_pattern: WeaponPattern  # only for weapons
var active_ability: AbilityDefinition  # only for artifacts
var blueprint_required: String = ""  # empty = no blueprint needed
```

### StatModifier (existing, extended)
```
enum StatType {
    MAX_HP, MOVE_SPEED, ATTACK_DAMAGE, ATTACK_SPEED,
    BULLET_SPEED, BULLET_COUNT, SPREAD_ANGLE, PIERCE_COUNT,
    BULLET_LIFETIME, DEFENSE, CRIT_CHANCE, CRIT_DAMAGE,
    GOLD_MULT, RELIC_MULT, DODGE_CHANCE, LIFE_STEAL
}
```

### MutationDefinition
```
class_name MutationDefinition extends Resource

enum MutationType {
    PROJECTILE_SPLIT,    # bullets split on hit
    BULLET_PIERCE,       # bullets pass through enemies
    LIFE_STEAL,          # heal on damage dealt
    DASH_SHOCKWAVE,      # damage on dash
    FIRE_TRAIL,          # leave fire behind while moving
    CHAIN_LIGHTNING,     # damage chains to nearby enemies
    EXPLODING_BULLETS,   # AoE on bullet impact
    FREEZE_AURA,         # slow nearby enemies
    RICOCHET,            # bullets bounce off walls
    VAMPIRIC_BURST,      # heal burst on kill
    HOMING_SHOTS,        # bullets seek enemies
    SHIELD_ON_KILL,      # temp shield per kill
}

var mutation_id: String
var mutation_name: String
var description: String
var type: MutationType
var icon: Texture2D
var tier: int = 1            # 1-3, higher = stronger
var strength: float = 1.0    # multiplier for effect
var max_stacks: int = 3      # how many times this can be picked
var tags: Array[String] = [] # for synergy detection
```

## Mutation Stacking

Mutations stack additively up to max_stacks.

```
# Example: picking LIFE_STEAL 3 times
# tier 1 = 3% heal per hit
# stacked x3 = 9% heal per hit

func get_mutation_strength(type: MutationType) -> float:
    var total: float = 0.0
    for m in active_mutations:
        if m.type == type:
            total += m.strength * m.tier
    return total
```

## Mutation Execution Pipeline

Mutations hook into combat events:

```
ON_BULLET_FIRE:
    → HOMING_SHOTS: set bullet.homing_strength
    → PROJECTILE_SPLIT: register split callback

ON_BULLET_HIT:
    → LIFE_STEAL: heal player
    → EXPLODING_BULLETS: spawn AoE
    → CHAIN_LIGHTNING: damage nearby enemies
    → PROJECTILE_SPLIT: spawn child bullets

ON_ENEMY_KILL:
    → VAMPIRIC_BURST: heal burst
    → SHIELD_ON_KILL: add temp shield

ON_PLAYER_DASH:
    → DASH_SHOCKWAVE: spawn damage wave

ON_PLAYER_MOVE:
    → FIRE_TRAIL: spawn fire hazard

ON_PLAYER_HIT:
    → DODGE_CHANCE: roll to negate
    → FREEZE_AURA: slow attacker
```

### MutationProcessor
```
class_name MutationProcessor extends Node

signal on_bullet_fire(bullet: Node2D)
signal on_bullet_hit(bullet: Node2D, target: Node2D)
signal on_enemy_kill(enemy: Node2D)
signal on_player_dash(position: Vector2)
signal on_player_move(position: Vector2, delta: float)
signal on_player_hit(damage: int, source: Node2D)

var active_mutations: Array[MutationDefinition] = []

func process_event(event: String, context: Dictionary) -> Dictionary:
    var result = context.duplicate()
    for mutation in active_mutations:
        result = _apply_mutation(mutation, event, result)
    return result
```

## Weapon-Pattern Relationship

Each weapon has an associated WeaponPattern:

| Weapon | Pattern | Base Stats |
|--------|---------|------------|
| Short Bow | Single Shot | fast rate, low damage |
| War Bow | Spread (3) | medium rate, medium damage |
| Staff of Storms | Ring (8) | slow rate, high damage |
| Twin Daggers | Burst (3) | very fast, very low damage |
| Cannon | Shotgun (5) | very slow, very high damage |
| Spirit Orb | Spiral | continuous, low damage |
| Crossbow | Parallel (2) | medium rate, medium damage |

Mutations modify the pattern output:
- PROJECTILE_SPLIT doubles bullet count on hit
- RICOCHET changes bullet behavior post-bounce
- HOMING adds tracking to all pattern bullets

## Blueprint System

```
class_name BlueprintDefinition extends Resource

var blueprint_id: String
var blueprint_name: String
var result_item: EquipmentDefinition
var relic_cost: int
var gold_cost: int
var discovered: bool = false
var crafted_count: int = 0

# Discovery sources
var drop_source: String  # "elite", "boss", "fortress_ice", etc.
var drop_chance: float = 0.1
```

### Blueprint Discovery Flow
```
Kill elite/boss OR conquer fortress
    ↓
Roll drop_chance against blueprint pool
    ↓
Blueprint added to player's collection (discovered = true)
    ↓
At base camp: craft item using relic_cost + gold_cost
    ↓
Item added to equipment pool (can now drop in dungeon runs)
```

## Synergy Tags

Items and mutations have tags that create synergies:

```
Tags: "fire", "ice", "lightning", "poison", "speed", "defense", "heal", "crit"

# Synergy detection
func get_active_synergies() -> Array[String]:
    var tag_counts: Dictionary = {}
    for m in active_mutations:
        for tag in m.tags:
            tag_counts[tag] = tag_counts.get(tag, 0) + 1

    var synergies: Array[String] = []
    for tag in tag_counts:
        if tag_counts[tag] >= 3:
            synergies.append(tag)
    return synergies

# 3+ fire tags = "Inferno" synergy → +30% fire damage
# 3+ speed tags = "Velocity" synergy → +20% move/attack speed
```

## Interactions With Other Systems

| System | Interaction |
|--------|-------------|
| Dungeon | Items drop from enemies, rewards, shops |
| Combat | Weapons define attack pattern, mutations hook into combat events |
| Companions | Core module can boost companion stats |
| Army | Equipment can be assigned to army divisions (different pool) |
| Economy | Blueprints cost relics + gold to craft |
| Overworld | Fortress conquests unlock biome-specific mutations |
| Analytics | Track mutation pick rates, synergy effectiveness, build archetypes |

## MVP Implementation Strategy

### MVP-1: Basic Equipment
- 3 weapons with distinct WeaponPatterns (single, spread, burst)
- Stat modifiers only (no mutations yet)
- Equipment drops from enemies and rewards
- 4 equipment slots functional

### MVP-2: Mutations
- 4 mutation types (pierce, life_steal, homing, exploding_bullets)
- Mutation shrines in dungeon
- Stacking system
- Visual feedback per mutation

### MVP-3: Full System
- All 12+ mutations
- Blueprint discovery and crafting
- Synergy detection
- Rarity tiers with visual distinction
- Weapon-specific mutation interactions
</file>

<file path="docs/design/OVERWORLD_SYSTEM.md">
# Overworld Conquest System

## Purpose
The overworld is the strategic metagame. A Risk-style territory map that gives long-term goals, unlocks new content, and makes dungeon runs feel purposeful. Conquest is persistent across deaths.

## Map Structure

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                OVERWORLD MAP                │
│                                             │
│   [Start] ── [Outpost] ── [Outpost]        │
│       │           │            │            │
│   [Outpost] ── [Stronghold] ── [Outpost]   │
│       │           │            │            │
│   [Outpost] ── [Outpost] ── [Stronghold]   │
│                   │            │            │
│            [Stronghold] ── [Outpost]        │
│                   │                         │
│            ★ [FORTRESS] ★                   │
│                                             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Territory Types

### Outpost
- **Difficulty**: Easy
- **Battle**: Auto-resolve (1 division)
- **Reward**: Small gold + troop tokens
- **Purpose**: Territory expansion, resource generation

### Stronghold
- **Difficulty**: Medium
- **Battle**: Tactical (1-2 divisions, choose formation)
- **Reward**: Moderate gold/relics + equipment blueprints
- **Purpose**: Gatekeeper to fortress zones

### Fortress
- **Difficulty**: Hard
- **Battle**: Multi-phase tactical (2-4 divisions)
- **Reward**: Major system unlocks
- **Purpose**: Primary progression milestones

## Data Models

### TerritoryDefinition
```
class_name TerritoryDefinition extends Resource

enum TerritoryType { OUTPOST, STRONGHOLD, FORTRESS }
enum Biome { PLAINS, FOREST, MOUNTAIN, DESERT, ICE, ANCIENT }
enum OwnerFaction { NEUTRAL, PLAYER, ENEMY_RED, ENEMY_BLUE, ENEMY_GREEN }

var territory_id: String
var territory_name: String
var type: TerritoryType
var biome: Biome
var map_position: Vector2     # position on overworld map

# Connections
var connected_territories: Array[String] = []  # territory_ids

# Combat
var garrison_divisions: Array[DivisionTemplate] = []
var difficulty_rating: int = 1  # 1-10

# Rewards
var gold_reward: int = 100
var relic_reward: int = 0
var troop_token_reward: int = 2
var blueprint_rewards: Array[String] = []
var system_unlock: String = ""  # "frost_mutations", "poison_items", etc.

# State
var owner: OwnerFaction = OwnerFaction.NEUTRAL
var conquered: bool = false
var turns_since_conquered: int = 0
```

### OverworldState
```
class_name OverworldState extends Resource

var territories: Dictionary = {}  # territory_id -> TerritoryState
var player_army: Array[Division] = []
var current_territory: String = "start"
var turn_number: int = 0
var territories_conquered: int = 0
```

### DivisionTemplate (for garrison enemies)
```
class_name DivisionTemplate extends Resource

var unit_composition: Dictionary = {}  # UnitType -> count
var formation: FormationDefinition
var power_rating: int = 100
```

## Map Traversal

```
Player can only attack territories connected to owned territories.

func get_attackable_territories() -> Array[String]:
    var attackable: Array[String] = []
    for tid in owned_territories:
        var territory = territories[tid]
        for connected in territory.connected_territories:
            if not is_owned(connected) and connected not in attackable:
                attackable.append(connected)
    return attackable
```

## Fortress Unlock Rewards

| Fortress | Biome | Unlocks |
|----------|-------|---------|
| Frostpeak Citadel | Ice | Frost mutations, ice weapons, Snow Archer unit |
| Venomspire Keep | Desert | Poison mutations, venom equipment, Scorpion Cavalry |
| Ancient Sanctum | Ancient | Legendary blueprints, Ancient Golem unit, relic doubler |
| Stormwall Bastion | Mountain | Lightning mutations, storm weapons, Thunder Siege |
| Shadowmere Fortress | Forest | Stealth mutations, shadow equipment, Assassin Infantry |

## Territory Passive Income

Owned territories generate resources per "turn" (after each dungeon run):

```
func calculate_passive_income() -> Dictionary:
    var income = {"gold": 0, "relics": 0, "troop_tokens": 0}
    for tid in owned_territories:
        var t = territories[tid]
        match t.type:
            TerritoryType.OUTPOST:
                income["gold"] += 25
                income["troop_tokens"] += 1
            TerritoryType.STRONGHOLD:
                income["gold"] += 75
                income["relics"] += 1
                income["troop_tokens"] += 2
            TerritoryType.FORTRESS:
                income["gold"] += 150
                income["relics"] += 3
                income["troop_tokens"] += 5
    return income
```

## Enemy Faction Counter-Attacks

After conquering N territories, enemy factions can counter-attack:

```
func check_counter_attack(turn: int) -> TerritoryDefinition:
    if turn % 5 != 0:  # every 5 turns
        return null

    var vulnerable = get_border_territories()  # player territories adjacent to enemy
    if vulnerable.is_empty():
        return null

    var target = vulnerable[randi() % vulnerable.size()]
    # Spawn counter-attack garrison
    target.garrison_divisions = generate_counter_army(turn)
    return target
```

## Interactions With Other Systems

| System | Interaction |
|--------|-------------|
| Army | Divisions deployed for territory battles |
| Economy | Territories generate passive income; battles cost/reward resources |
| Dungeon | Each death completes a "turn"; fortress unlocks expand dungeon content |
| Blueprints | Fortresses unlock biome-specific blueprints |
| Analytics | Track territory difficulty ratings, conquest order, counter-attack survival |

## MVP Implementation Strategy

### MVP-1: Linear Map
- 5 territories in a line (3 outposts, 1 stronghold, 1 fortress)
- Auto-resolve all battles
- Territory conquering unlocks next node
- Passive income after each run

### MVP-2: Branching Map
- 12-15 territories with branching paths
- Tactical battles for strongholds/fortresses
- Fortress unlock rewards
- Enemy counter-attacks

### MVP-3: Full Map
- 20+ territories across 5 biomes
- Multiple fortresses with unique unlocks
- Faction AI with expansion behavior
- Dynamic difficulty based on player progression
- Map visual with fog of war
</file>

